\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Splendour of God's glory bright,
\par O Thou that bringest light from light,
\par O Light of light, light's living spring,
\par O Day, all days illumining.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O Thou true Sun, on us Thy glance
\par Let fall in royal radiance,
\par The Spirit's sanctifying beam
\par Upon our earthly senses stream.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The Father, too, our prayers implore,
\par Father of glory evermore;
\par The Father of all grace and might,
\par To banish sin from our delight:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. To guide whate'er we nobly do,
\par With love all envy to subdue,
\par To make ill- fortune turn to fair,
\par And give us grace our wrongs to bear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Our mind be in His keeping placed,
\par Our body true to Him and chaste,
\par Where only faith her fire shall feed,
\par To burn the tares of Satan's seed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. And Christ to us for food shall be,
\par From Him our drink that welleth free,
\par The Spirit's wine, that maketh whole,
\par And, mocking not, exalts the soul.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Rejoicing may this day go hence,
\par Like virgin dawn our innocence,
\par Like fiery moon our faith appear,
\par Nor know the gloom of twilight drear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Morn in her rosy car is borne;
\par Let Him come forth, our perfect Morn,
\par The Word in God the Father one,
\par The Father perfect in the Son.
\par                               Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

